#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059469 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/id #uuid "d2698dbf-dea6-5abb-970e-a3ace180e337" :question/math-academy-id "e-4341" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3 & - 4 & 1 \\\\ - 7 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{i} - \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & 1 \\\\ - 7 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{j} + \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & - 4 \\\\ - 7 & 0\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = ( ( - 4 ) \\cdot  2 - 1 \\cdot  0 ) \\mathbf{i} - ( 3 \\cdot  2 - 1 \\cdot  ( - 7 ) ) \\mathbf{j} + ( 3 \\cdot  0 - ( - 4 ) \\cdot  ( - 7 ) ) \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = - 8 \\mathbf{i} - 13 \\mathbf{j} - 28 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - 8 , - 13 , - 28 \\rangle  .\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059470 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/id #uuid "b834e666-de4f-5964-a280-6571ad44b6bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4343" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle$, and $\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\, \\mid = \\sqrt{19}$. Find $x$." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 2 x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{i} - \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & 2 x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{j} + \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = - x \\mathbf{i} - 3 x \\mathbf{j} + 3 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - x , - 3 x , 3 \\rangle  .\\end{array}$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}| \\, \\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} \\, | & = \\sqrt{( - x {)}^{2} + ( - 3 x {)}^{2} + {3}^{2}} \\\\  & = \\sqrt{10 {x}^{2} + 9} .\\end{array}$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl} & | \\, \\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} \\, | = \\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10 {x}^{2} + 9} = \\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10 {x}^{2} + 9 = 19 \\\\  & 10 {x}^{2} = 10 \\\\  & {x}^{2} = 1\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1$."}]}
